.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt FIL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fil
.Nd scan disk usage and clean caches on macOS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm scan
.Op Ar DIR
.Op Fl j Ar N
.Op Fl -private
.Op Fl -full
.Op Fl -top Ar N
.Op Fl -naive
.Op Fl -porcelain
.Op Fl -tolerant-hardlinks
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl -no-color
.Nm
.Cm doctor
.Op Fl -no-open
.Op Fl -no-color
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl -home Ar DIR
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -timings
.Op Fl -no-color
.Nm
.Cm clean
.Ar id | rule ...
.Op Fl -home Ar DIR
.Op Fl -yes
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -timings
.Op Fl -no-color
.Nm
.Cm completion
.Ar zsh | bash | fish
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Op Fl V | -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a fast disk scanner and cleaner.
.Cm scan
sizes a directory in on-disk bytes, counting each APFS clone family once.
.Cm list
and
.Cm clean
find and remove caches, build output and other files that can be recreated.
.Pp
Options and operands can come in any order.
.Fl h
or
.Fl -help
after a command prints that command's help.
A command accepts only its own options; anything else is a usage error.
.Fl -
ends option parsing, so a directory whose name starts with a dash
can be scanned.
.Pp
Output is styled (colour, live progress on standard error) only on a terminal.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm Cm scan Op Ar DIR
Scan a directory and print its size.
The default is the home folder.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl j Ar N
Worker threads, a whole number from 1 to 64.
.It Fl -private
Size in private (non-shared) bytes.
.It Fl -full
Ignore the snapshot and scan from scratch.
.It Fl -top Ar N
List the N largest directories; 0 lists none.
The default is 15.
.It Fl -naive
Time a plain
.Li FileManager
walk instead.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl -porcelain .
.It Fl -porcelain
Print one machine-readable line.
See
.Sx OUTPUT .
.It Fl -tolerant-hardlinks
Count unknown hard links and report them as uncertain.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
No warning about folders that could not be read.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Show timing details and skipped-entry counts.
.It Fl -no-color
Plain output, also when
.Ev NO_COLOR
is set or standard output is not a terminal.
.El
.It Nm Cm doctor
Check whether the terminal app has Full Disk Access.
Without it, some folders cannot be read and scan sizes come out too low.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -no-open
Only print; do not open System Settings.
.It Fl -no-color
Plain output.
.El
.It Nm Cm list
List cleanup candidates in the home folder.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -home Ar DIR
Use
.Ar DIR
instead of the home folder.
.It Fl -json
Machine-readable output.
.It Fl -timings
Phase and rule timings on standard error.
.It Fl -no-color
Plain output.
.El
.It Nm Cm clean Ar id | rule ...
Clean candidates.
This is a dry run unless
.Fl -yes
is given.
A rule id selects its safe and review items;
name a careful item by its candidate id.
Most items move to the Trash.
Some rules run the tool's own removal command, which is permanent;
a dry run shows it as
.Dq would run: .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -home Ar DIR
Use
.Ar DIR
instead of the home folder.
.It Fl -yes
Clean for real.
.It Fl -json
Machine-readable output.
.It Fl -timings
Phase and rule timings on standard error.
.It Fl -no-color
Plain output.
.El
.It Nm Cm completion Ar shell
Print a completion script for zsh, bash or fish on standard output.
.It Nm Cm help Op Ar command
Show help for a command.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show the main help.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
.Nm Cm scan Fl -porcelain
prints one line of
.Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value
pairs separated by spaces:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li mode
.Li full
or
.Li incremental .
.It Li alloc
Allocated bytes, as
.Xr du 1
counts them.
With
.Fl -private ,
private bytes.
.It Li logical
Sum of logical file sizes.
.It Li files
Files counted, hard links once.
.It Li dirs
Directories, including the root.
.It Li uncertain
Only with
.Fl -tolerant-hardlinks :
bytes of hard links that may be counted twice.
.It Li cloneaware
Allocated bytes with each APFS clone family counted once.
.It Li shared
Not with
.Fl -private :
bytes
.Xr du 1
counts again for clones.
.It Li unreadable
Folders that could not be read.
.El
.Pp
Fields are only ever appended, never removed, renamed or reordered.
Read them by key, because
.Li uncertain
and
.Li shared
are conditional.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, output has no colour.
.It Ev TERM
Output has no colour when it is
.Li dumb .
.It Ev FIL_SNAPSHOT_DIR
Directory for snapshots instead of the user's cache folder.
Meant for tests.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/Library/Caches/com.vucod.Fil/snapshots/
One snapshot per scanned root, used to update a scan incrementally.
.It Pa ~/Library/Caches/com.vucod.Fil/snapshots/tool-paths.json
Cache locations reported by tools such as npm and pip.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li 0
Success.
.It Li 1
Error: a directory is missing or not a directory,
.Cm clean
matches nothing, or
.Cm doctor
finds Full Disk Access missing or unknown.
.It Li 2
Usage error: unknown command or option, missing or invalid value,
more than one directory,
an unknown shell for
.Cm completion .
.It Li 3
.Cm clean Fl -yes :
one or more items failed.
Others may have succeeded.
.It Li 130
.Cm clean Fl -yes
was interrupted with Ctrl-C.
The remaining items were not touched.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr du 1
